From: HardDinD developers
Subject: [EXPERIMENT] um: cache scrubbed mapping brokers, never user runners

Bound the cache to four inactive brokers. Reap all user runners and
synchronously unmap guest memory and runner slots before reuse. Keep
cached brokers in child-death tracking and drain them on shutdown.
Default off; requires shared-VM runners. No guest syscall is bypassed.

--- a/arch/um/include/shared/skas/skas.h
+++ b/arch/um/include/shared/skas/skas.h
